SubVox
Copyright 2026 Aetherion Substrata Ltd

SubVox is a native Windows text-to-speech engine for the Phonon 31M model,
written in .lx and driving the GPU directly through Direct3D 11.

Third-party material included or adapted (all Apache License 2.0):

- Phonon 31M English model, tokenizer and voice catalog by Gradium
  (https://gradium.ai): https://huggingface.co/gradium/phonon-31m-en and
  https://huggingface.co/gradium/phonon-voices. The model file in model/ is the
  8-bit conversion published at https://huggingface.co/blixt/phonon-31m-en-webgpu.
- GPU compute shaders ported from "Phonon on WebGPU", Copyright 2026 Blixt.
- Phonon builds on Pocket TTS and the Mimi codec by Kyutai (https://kyutai.org).

SubVox is an independent engine. It is not made or endorsed by Gradium.
